  "findings": [
    "Revised EgoHand improves wrist disagreement and unknown added-correction failures relative to legacyEgo. It still has more MP-referenced visible finger-motion failures and worse right-hand holdout image-reference distance than the finalsame-cropMP control.",
    "Global native updates are nonzero in both fits, but revised left finger/arm controls at60/110/308 are exactly originalSAM baseline. Reduced hidden-hand changes are abstention from unsupported updates, not recovered true hidden motion.",
    "Proposal wrist projection and native depth agreement partly follow the retarget construction using shared trainingMP wrist/native baseline depth. Their improvement is engineering consistency, not independent wrist/depth accuracy.",
    "At60/110/285, orange generated proposals can be caused by stride5 exclusion even on a visible hand. Orange is not an occlusion/detection-failure label.",
    "Native opening remains nonconstant; the right-hand release-window median/range differs from samecropMP and needs source-image inspection. Neither nonzero variation nor lower self-motion proves preservation of real grasp timing.",
    "Historical oldEgo-to-newEgo changes combine crops, retargeting and admission. SamecropMP is the primary controlled observer comparison; no single-intervention causal claim is supported."
  ],
